{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_syllabus","statement":"The instructors for the course are Prof. Charles Caldart and Prof. Nicholas Ashford.","source_span":"Instructors\nProf. Charles Caldart\nProf. Nicholas Ashford"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_syllabus","statement":"Lectures meet 1 session per week for 3 hours per session.","source_span":"Lectures: 1 session / week, 3 hours / session"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_syllabus","statement":"Grading is Class Participation 15%, Writing Assignment 15%, Midterm 35%, and Second Exam 35%.","source_span":"Class Participation\n15%\nWriting Assignment\n15%\nMidterm\n35%\nSecond Exam\n35%"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_syllabus","statement":"The writing assignment is around 5 pages, and everyone is asked to respond to the same question.","source_span":"a relatively short (around 5 pages) writing assignment ... Everyone will be asked to respond to the same question."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_syllabus","statement":"The course has a midterm and a non-cumulative second exam.","source_span":"a midterm, and a (non-cumulative) second exam"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_syllabus","statement":"The required textbook is Ashford, Nicholas A., and Charles C. Caldart, 'Technology, Law and the Working Environment,' Revised ed., Washington DC: Island Press, 1996, ISBN 9781559634465.","source_span":"Technology, Law and the Working Environment. Revised ed. Washington, DC: Island Press, 1996. ISBN: 9781559634465."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_syllabus","statement":"A second source of course materials is galleys from the forthcoming book 'Environmental Law, Policy, and Economics' by Ashford and Caldart, forthcoming in 2007.","source_span":"Environmental Law, Policy, and Economics. (Forthcoming 2007)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d1_10-805j-technology-law-and-the-working-e_syllabus","statement":"The course covers regulation of toxic substances affecting worker health and safety, economics of health and safety, labor and anti-discrimination law, worker right-to-know, and workers' compensation.","source_span":"the regulation of toxic substances and processes that affect the health and safety of workers, the economics of health and safety, labor and anti-discrimination law, worker right-to-know, and workers' compensation"}
